spans.s:
hṛt, a. (—˚) bringing;
 stealing, robbing;
 🞄taking away, dispelling, putting an end to.

hṛta-dravya, a. robbed of oneʼs property;
 🞄-vāsas, a. bereft of oneʼs garment;
 🞄-śiṣṭa, pp. spared from pillage;
 -sarvasva, 🞄a. bereft of oneʼs all;
 -sāra, a. robbed of the 🞄best part.

hṛt-tás, ad. from the heart (RV.¹);
 🞄-padma, n. lotus of the heart;
 -sphoṭa, m. 🞄breaking of the heart, broken heart: -m, ad. 🞄of a broken heart (die).
